    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nA structured address form on `POST /api/owners`, keeping the flat `address` input working.\n\n**Files touched (4):**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `addressLine1` and optional `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (so they appear on both request and the `Owner` response via `allOf`), and dropped `address` from the `required` list. `city`/`postcode` were already present.\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/owner/AddressNormalizer.java`** \u2014 added a small `compose(line1, line2)` helper: the normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space and the normalized `addressLine2` appended only when `addressLine2` is present.\n\n3. **`.../rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 when `addressLine1` is non-blank, the effective address is `compose(...)`; otherwise it falls back to normalizing the flat `address`. The existing required-field check now validates that composed value, so an owner is valid with either form plus `city`. When structured, it also stores the normalized `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` on the owner.\n\n4. **`.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` as `@Transient` fields with plain accessors (MapStruct auto-maps them onto the response DTO).\n\n## Design notes\n\n- **Household hash / postcode validation / locality need no change**: they read `postcode` and `city`, which are top-level fields supplied identically in both forms, so they already use the structured input, with the persisted flat `address` as the natural fallback on reload.\n- **Why `@Transient`**: the composed `address` is a real, persisted column (the durable output). The line fields are echoed within the request context; the test profile (`ddl-auto=none`, positional `INSERT`s in `data.sql`) meant persisting them would have forced edits to `schema.sql` plus every owner row in `data.sql` \u2014 far more structural impact for behaviour the spec already covers via the persisted composed `address`. On a later reload the structured fields are absent and callers fall back to the flat `address`, consistent with the \"falling back to the flat address\" contract.\n- No existing methods in the large `Owner` class or the `OwnerMapper` were modified \u2014 only additive accessors and a helper in a tiny class, keeping per-function complexity low.\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
